---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { LAST_UPDATED, AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, AUTHOR_ROLE } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { organizationSchema, breadcrumbSchema, profilePageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { PAGES } from '../../lib/guides';
import { helpers } from '../../lib/helpers';
const lang = 'en';
const h = helpers(lang);
const n = PAGES.length + 1;
---
<PageLayout title="Citizenship Test Free publisher: who writes the questions" description="Who publishes Citizenship Test Free, where its USCIS civics questions, English practice sentences, N-400 dates and fees come from, and what it never sells." lang={lang} jsonLd={[organizationSchema(lang), profilePageSchema({ path: route('about', lang), lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'About', path: route('about', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><p class="kicker">About</p><h1 class="mt-0 text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Who is behind Citizenship Test Free</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <div class="not-prose mb-6"><p class="text-lg font-semibold text-navy-900">{AUTHOR_NAME}</p><p class="text-navy-700">{AUTHOR_ROLE[lang]}</p></div>
    <p>Citizenship Test Free is published by Radif Partners, a company that builds free tools on public rules and public data. It is meant for green card holders in the United States who are getting ready to become citizens: they need to pass the English and civics tests at the naturalization interview, and before that, to know the first day USCIS will accept their Form N-400.</p>
    <h2>What the site does</h2>
    <p>It gives the civics interview as USCIS runs it, with the official questions of the 2025 and 2008 lists, the officer's stop rule ({h.P.us.test2025.passCorrect} right or {h.P.us.test2025.failWrong} wrong on the 2025 test), the 65/20 list, English reading and dictation built on the official vocabulary, every question in Spanish too, the earliest N-400 filing date and the N-400 fee. Every practice answer shows all the wordings USCIS accepts. And it does what the official early filing calculator does not: from your green card date and every trip, past or planned, it finds the earliest day you can file, checking continuous residence and physical presence day by day with the counting rule of the USCIS Policy Manual. It also adds up the N-400 fee for a whole household and tells you whether the reduced fee or a waiver applies.</p>
    <p>Everything is free, without an account, an email address or a premium tier, and nothing you type leaves your browser.</p>
    <h2>Where the questions and rules come from</h2>
    <p>The U.S. civics questions and answers are the official USCIS lists, in the public domain, copied without change; the 2008 list in Spanish is the official USCIS translation, the 2025 list in Spanish is our own unofficial translation, and the answer choices and English practice sentences are ours. Fees, test formats, residence rules and processing times were read on uscis.gov, in the USCIS Policy Manual and in the Federal Register, and each page links to the page it was read on. The <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a> gives the details, including the cases where two official pages disagree.</p>
    <h2>What we are not</h2>
    <p>We are not USCIS or any part of the U.S. government, nor a law firm or an accredited representative. We cannot schedule an interview, take an application or look at a file, and the practice answer choices are ours, not the officer's. The site uses no seal or official logo. For advice on a particular case, the official pages list who is allowed to give it.</p>
    <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
    <p>The site sells no course, book, app or legal service, takes no commission and links to no firm that does. If advertising is added one day, it will never sit above a test, and it cannot use your answers because they stay in your browser.</p>
    <h2>Tell us when something is wrong</h2>
    <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the rule, or the number of the question and its list. The <a href={route('editorial', lang)}>editorial policy</a> explains how a correction is made. The site has {n} pages in English.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-600">Rules and fees last checked on <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, 'en-GB')}</time>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
